      'His words are from The Burden of Freedom (Creation House, 2000), quoted briefly and cited by chapter. The dog-conditioning experiment is his illustration: he credits a report in a science journal but gives no citation, so it is told as his story, not as established science. His book states that British slavery was abolished in 1827; the record shows slavery in The Bahamas ended with abolition across the British Empire on 1 August 1834, so that date is not repeated here. His line that poverty is ultimately a product of mismanagement is weighed in the lesson: Scripture names both mismanagement and injustice as causes of poverty. The publisher’s description is attributed to the publisher.',
