    bigIdea:
      'In Overcoming Crisis, published in 2009 under a first chapter titled Global Crisis, Personal Crisis, Dr. Myles Munroe argued that a crisis is an event you could not control or prepare for, but your response to it can be managed, and that management was humanity’s first assignment: Yahweh did not send rain on the earth until there was a man to work the ground. With Joseph as his model, he taught that the secret to thriving, not just surviving, in a crisis is effective management, and that effective management implies trust in Yahweh.',
    inApp:
      'Read chapters 1, 3, 6 and 7 of Overcoming Crisis (Destiny Image, 2009) in a licensed copy, then read Joseph’s story in Genesis 39-41 and 50. Weigh it by the Word: Genesis 2:5 and 2:15, Genesis 41:33-38, Luke 16:10, 1 Corinthians 4:2 and Genesis 50:20, and write down what you can manage in your crisis this week.',
