      'In The Purpose and Power of Praise and Worship Dr. Myles Munroe taught that praise is celebrating Yahweh as our heart’s true home: commending Him, which means entrusting ourselves to His care and recommending Him to others, approving and glorifying Him. He argued that praise is a conscious choice of the will, a willing sacrifice, and an expression of faith, not a warm-up before the sermon, and that praise that flows from knowing Him is bragging about Yahweh instead of ourselves.',
