    honestNote:
      'His words are from The Purpose and Power of Praise and Worship (Destiny Image, 2000), quoted briefly and cited by printed page. The definitions of praise and commend are ones he takes from Webster’s dictionary, as he says. Scripture inside his book is in the translations he printed (mostly NIV, with some KJV); this lesson quotes Scripture only in the KJV. One of his phrases in the chapter, that Yahweh needs us to provide a dwelling place for Him and that praise is that altar, is weighed in the lesson by Acts 17:24-25 and Psalm 22:3: Yahweh needs nothing from us, yet He is enthroned on the praises of His people. Chapter 5 is the lesson’s focus; the other chapters are named from the contents, not summarized.',
